{"profile":{"name":"Stephen Holyday","ward":"Ward 2, Etobicoke Centre","bio":"Stephen Holyday has been Toronto's councillor for Etobicoke Centre since December 2014, serving Ward 3 from 2014-2018 and Ward 2 since the 2018 boundary changes; he was re-elected in 2022 with 72.28% of the vote. Before entering politics he spent 15 years (1999-2014) as a manager at the Ontario Ministry of Energy, and he holds a Bachelor of Technology in Architectural Science from Ryerson University. He is the son of Doug Holyday, a former Etobicoke mayor and Ward 3 councillor, and previously served as Deputy Mayor (2017, and again 2018-2022).","committees":["Etobicoke York Community Council (Chair)","Audit Committee (Chair)","Service Excellence Committee (Chair)","General Government Committee (Vice-Chair)","Hockey Hall of Fame Board of Directors","Canadian National Exhibition Association (Vice-President)","Heritage Toronto"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_holyday@toronto.ca","phone":"416-392-4002"},"promises":[{"text":"Reduce traffic congestion in Etobicoke Centre.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_Toronto_municipal_election"},{"text":"Invest in transit infrastructure to serve the growing population.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2014_Toronto_municipal_election"}]},"lobbying":{"total":998,"term":262,"first":"2014-12-02","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":232,"clients":178,"subjects":427,"methods":{"Meetings":363,"Emails":458,"Phone calls":95,"Written":45,"Other or unreported":37},"top":[{"label":"Economic Development","count":235},{"label":"By-law / Regulation","count":198},{"label":"Licences / Licensing","count":157},{"label":"Planning and Development Application, Zoning By-law","count":103},{"label":"Attractions / Tourism","count":76}],"years":[{"year":2014,"count":5},{"year":2015,"count":116},{"year":2016,"count":107},{"year":2017,"count":82},{"year":2018,"count":49},{"year":2019,"count":145},{"year":2020,"count":70},{"year":2021,"count":113},{"year":2022,"count":70